                <pb facs="0779" n="703" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/965: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-29T13:00:00+00:00">April 29, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 29—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Department’s telegram No. 19, April 24, 1 p.m. Fact that Franco-Spanish
                    commercial negotiations have again been broken off makes present moment
                    singularly opportune to hasten our own negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
